  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Action by Ethnic Minorities in the Mekong</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MekongElevate will strengthen the climate resilience of upland communities, particularly ethnic minority women, youth and people with disability, across two economically and environmentally interconnected regions of Cambodia, Laos, and Vietnam. The program adopts an integrated approach that promotes Climate-Smart Agriculture and adaptation innovations, strengthens mechanisms for addressing climate-induced Loss and Damage and enhances community safety nets. This approach aims to build more resilient communities capable of adapting to, mitigating, and recovering from climate impacts, while addressing the gender, disability and social inequities that perpetuate vulnerability. The investment will be implemented in partnership with CARE through the Mekong-Australia Partnership (MAP).</narrative>
  </description>
